Source: typst
Section: text
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Krysztal Huang <krysztal.huang@outlook.com>
Build-Depends:
 {{RUST_PACKAGE_NAME}} (= {{RUST_PACKAGE_VERSION}}),
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 libssl-dev,
 pkgconf,
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: {{SOURCE_GIT}}
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: typst
Architecture: any
Depends: ca-certificates, ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: markup-based typesetting system
 Typst is a markup-based typesetting system designed to be as powerful as
 LaTeX while being much easier to learn and use. It provides built-in markup
 for common formatting tasks, flexible functions for everything else, a
 tightly integrated scripting system, math typesetting, bibliography
 management, and fast compile times thanks to incremental compilation.
 .
 This package ships the typst command line compiler with man pages and
 shell completions. The self-update feature is disabled; package upgrades
 are managed by APT.
